pointer-motion

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Move the pointer along its easing in time instead of along the inverse of it, add a Hand easing measured from real pointing strokes, and keep the drawn pointer on the events' clock after a Wait.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream evp samples pointer moves by time and keeps the drawn pointer on the event clock after a Wait.
